&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to integrate avionics and mission systems into air vehicles effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and modify 3D CAD models and 2D drawings for secondary structures and system components, including large assembly model management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct simulations and analyses, including hand calculations and FEA (finite element analysis), to validate designs against performance requirements and regulatory standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes, analyze failures, and transition successful projects into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design reviews, perform analyses, visit vendors, and define and execute hardware test plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support critical hardware demonstrations for customers as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to test sites or vendor facilities as needed to support development and integration efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Aerospace Engineering or Mechanical Engineering, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in air vehicle systems integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with hypersonic missiles and military standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Siemens NX CAD software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, collaboration, and teamwork skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;U.S. citizenship and eligibility to obtain and maintain a Secret security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) tools such as Teamcenter or Windchill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret DoD clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with unmanned air vehicle (UAV) design and development.&lt;/li&gt;
