&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are seeking a highly experienced and results-oriented Staff Technical Program Manager (TPM) to join our TPM organization. Our mission is to improve engineering velocity, and you will act as a force multiplier on mission-critical, large, complex initiatives with a high degree of cross-functional collaboration. This role requires a balance of software engineering expertise, &amp;nbsp;leadership, and the ability to drive programs that align with both technical and business goals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth to fully comprehend the nuances of software architecture, design and implementation in Cloud / SaaS / Enterprise domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in TPM or Engineering management, with a focus on software development or infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successfully delivering complex roadmaps in fast-paced environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective at developing roadmaps, able to guide teams through planning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset, brings data-driven decision making to drive program improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with risk and dependency management, prioritization, conflict resolution, and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills, ability to influence and drive consensus across diverse teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software development methodologies (Agile, Scrum, Waterfall).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with project management tools (e.g., Linear, Jira, Asana).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a data, analytics, or business intelligence domain, ideally AI / LLM exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background (e.g., former engineer, technical degree).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications in project management (e.g., SAFe).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Programs: Drive end-to-end technical programs, ensuring alignment with business objectives and technical execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align Roadmaps: Deeply understand technical roadmaps, align with business goals for timely product delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve Problems: Resolve project-level issues, manage scope changes, and mitigate risks for smooth delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate: Partner with multiple teams across Engineering, Product and other functions, and TPM peers, to ensure effective execution of projects and resolution of dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share Information: Define and track KPIs, report progress and escalate issues to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve Process: Optimize processes, refine tools, and implement best practices for efficient program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead &amp;amp; Mentor: Lead teams and mentor junior program managers for growth and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For base compensation, we set standard ranges for all roles based on function and level benchmarked against similar stage growth companies and internal comparables. In order to be compliant with local legislation, as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, we share salary ranges on all job postings regardless of desired hiring location. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including candidate experience/expertise and may vary from the amounts listed below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may also be offered a performance-based bonus, equity, and a generous benefits program.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$183,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$252,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;AlphaSense is an equal-opportunity employer. We are committed to a work environment that supports, inspires, and respects all individuals. All employees share in the responsibility for fulfilling AlphaSense’s commitment to equal employment opportunity. AlphaSense does not discriminate against any employee or applicant on the basis of race, color, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, age, religion, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, military or veteran status, disability, or any other non-merit factor. This policy applies to every aspect of employment at AlphaSense, including recruitment, hiring, training, advancement, and termination.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;In addition, it is the policy of AlphaSense to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified employees who have protected disabilities to the extent required by applicable laws, regulations, and ordinances where a particular employee works.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
